body:
Note that there's an unfortunate condition here that I can't see being easily worked around: mismatched tags. This assert only works if the passed type is a `class`; `struct` and `union` will both fail. This means that either the forwawrd-declaration needs to be removed, or additional specializations are required:
```suggestion
/// Enforces the requirement that a type is not fully defined.
/// This can be used to reduce include coupling and keep compile times low.
/// The check must be made at the top of the corresponding .cpp file of a header.
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_CLASS(m_type) \
	class m_type;                              \
	static_assert(!is_fully_defined_v<m_type>, #m_type " was unexpectedly fully defined. Please check the include hierarchy of '" __FILE__ "' and remove includes that resolve the class.");
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_STRUCT(m_type) \
	struct m_type;                              \
	static_assert(!is_fully_defined_v<m_type>, #m_type " was unexpectedly fully defined. Please check the include hierarchy of '" __FILE__ "' and remove includes that resolve the struct.");
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_UNION(m_type) \
	union m_type;                              \
	static_assert(!is_fully_defined_v<m_type>, #m_type " was unexpectedly fully defined. Please check the include hierarchy of '" __FILE__ "' and remove includes that resolve the union.");
#else
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_CLASS(m_type)
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_STRUCT(m_type)
#define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_UNION(m_type)
```
